# Wave B showcase: glTF loading, sprites, text, particles and full
# keyframe tracks, together in one scene (plus Wave A carry-over: PBR
# standard materials under a directional light).
# A gold pyramid loaded from a glTF file stands beside a standard-
# material cube (spinning) and sphere (moved by a keyframe track);
# a billboard sprite floats above it, a particle fountain plays in
# front, and bitmap text names the engine overhead.
# Run: python3 tools/f3dc/f3dc.py run examples/waveb-showcase.f3d
# (2 seconds at 15 fps = 30 frames, 320x240, into build/)
scene "waveb-showcase" size 320 240 background black
camera at 5 3 8 look 0 0 0
light directional dir -0.5 -1 -0.7 strength 1.2
plane ground gray at 0 -2 0 size 20 material standard metalness 0 roughness 0.95
cube standard_cube red at -3 -1.25 0 size 1.5 material standard metalness 0 roughness 0.6
sphere mover blue at 0 -1.2 0 radius 0.8 material standard metalness 0 roughness 0.25
load "assets/pyramid.gltf" pyramid at 3.2 -1 0
sprite star at 3.2 1.4 0 size 1 color yellow
text banner "FORGE 3D" at -2.3 2.3 0 size 0.7 color white
particles fountain at 0 -2 2 count 60 life 2 speed 3 size 0.15 color orange spread 0.5 gravity 4 seed 7
keys mover duration 2 loop pingpong
key mover at 0 pos 0 -1.2 0 rot 0 0 0 scale 1
key mover at 1 pos 1.5 -0.2 0 rot 0 90 0 scale 1.2 ease smooth
key mover at 2 pos 0 -1.2 0 rot 0 180 0 scale 1
animate standard_cube spin y speed 90 duration 2 fps 15
render duration 2 fps 15
